flowchart TB
  accTitle: QuantumComputinglib textbooks and shared Lean foundations
  accDescr: External Lean references enter shared foundations only through reviewed reuse or narrow adapters. The textbooks reuse these foundations. State Preparation and Block Encoding are the current core; Quantum Information and Scientific Computing are planned extensions. Conditional algorithm and theory support lead into Scientific Computing. These are curriculum relationships, not Lean theorem implications.

  EXT["External Lean references<br/>Mathlib · attributed quantum Lean libraries<br/>upstream references, not automatic local proofs"]
  CORE["Shared Lean foundations<br/>Reviewed building blocks reused across textbooks<br/>linear algebra · states/tensors · operators<br/>circuits/registers · norms · resource interfaces"]

  subgraph TEXTBOOK["QuantumComputinglib textbooks"]
    direction TB
    subgraph CURRENT["Current core · compiled guided chapters"]
      direction LR
      SP["Part I · State Preparation<br/>U|0^n⟩ = |ψ⟩"]
      BE["Part II · Block Encoding<br/>‖A - αΠUΠ†‖ ≤ ε"]
    end
    subgraph PLANNED["Planned extensions · local chapter admission required"]
      direction TB
      QIT["Planned Part III · Quantum Information<br/>and Representation Theory<br/>symmetry · Schur–Weyl · de Finetti"]
      SCI["Planned Part IV · Quantum Scientific Computing<br/>QSP/QSVT · simulation · estimation<br/>linear systems · dynamics · open systems"]
    end
  end

  EXT -. "reviewed reuse / narrow adapters" .-> CORE
  CORE -->|common foundation| TEXTBOOK
  BE -. "algorithm support" .-> SCI
  QIT -. "theoretical support" .-> SCI

  classDef core fill:#f8f5ee,stroke:#826a32,color:#222222,stroke-width:1.5px;
  classDef state fill:#edf5f1,stroke:#2f7355,color:#18382b,stroke-width:1.5px;
  classDef block fill:#eef3f7,stroke:#49677d,color:#1f2e39,stroke-width:1.5px;
  classDef future fill:#f7f4fb,stroke:#735a8f,color:#2f2440,stroke-width:1.5px;
  classDef external fill:#ffffff,stroke:#64747a,color:#222222,stroke-width:1.25px;
  class CORE core;
  class SP state;
  class BE block;
  class QIT,SCI future;
  class EXT external;
